      "evidence": "tests/test_central_dogfood_lifecycle.py and tests/test_deepseek_harness_runtime.py: `if (ROOT / \".dev-platform.toml\").read_text(...) == (ROOT / \"dev-platform\" / \"source-contract.toml\").read_text(...): self.skipTest(...)`.",
      "id": "central-config-skip-unguarded-read",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "The new skip guard in two central-config tests reads dev-platform/source-contract.toml unconditionally. It raises FileNotFoundError, with no explicit message, if that file is absent. It also makes the tests skip in any checkout where the two files are byte-identical, which weakens the central-config assertion."
    },
    {
      "evidence": "tests/test_lifecycle_workers.py: `def setUpModule(): sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / \"template\" / \"scripts\"))`, with no teardown.",
      "id": "setupmodule-syspath-hack",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "The test fix inserts template/scripts at the front of sys.path in setUpModule and never removes it. This works around import-order pollution from other test modules and can mask the same ordering fragility elsewhere. It leaks global state across test modules."
    },
    {
      "evidence": "template/scripts/post_review_finalization.py `checks_env`: `env[\"PYTHONUSERBASE\"] = site.getuserbase()`.",
      "id": "checks-env-pins-operator-user-base",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "Finalization's harness-run selected checks now see the operator's Python user site (`PYTHONUSERBASE=site.getuserbase()`). This lets operator-installed packages influence check results and weakens the isolation of the credential-free scratch home. The design documents this as intentional, but it makes finalize results machine-dependent."
    }
